# The languages Skwir offers (ADR-139, 13): Automatic speaks them, and the
# Language setting lists them by their names alone, or as a draft. Any
# other language a catalog is in is listed as incomplete, with its share,
# for whoever chooses it, and Automatic never picks it.
#
# One tag a line, as its catalogs are named (fr), followed by `draft` while
# it is offered as one. `just words` writes a language here as a draft once
# 90% of all Skwir's messages are translated in it, and every message of
# what is on by default is: the program's own crates (core, the platform,
# the window, the host of plugins from outside) and each plugin on by
# default. Automatic then speaks it, and the window says once that it is a
# draft, About while it speaks it. `just words` takes its `draft` away once
# as much is reviewed (a message is reviewed once the `# draft` above it is
# gone).
#
# Only a person takes a language out, which lists it as incomplete again:
# a release refuses one here with less than 75% of its messages reviewed,
# and one here as a draft short of the draft's bar (`just words
# --release`: new messages are drafted before a release), while between
# releases each stays offered, what it lacks said in English. Its line
# comes back only once it meets a bar again.
fr draft
zh-Hans draft
